# Seen (bridge captures of the pie, map and hierarchy pages, then a real Home > Refresh + Ctrl+S with the matrix expanded and the slicer deliberately not): all seven predictions held. Every legend value drew on all four types, including the two positions no earlier probe had seen on them — 'Bottom' and 'Left' on pie and donut, 'Left' on scatter and map — and legend: off left no legend. labels on/off showed and removed the detail labels on pie and donut. The matrix bound to Sales[Geography] expanded Country to Region (FR 200 -> East 150, West 50; total 500) and the slicer showed Country, Region with expanders, both straight from a spec. The save changed NO option object and NO projection Blueprint wrote: only Desktop's own additions — "active": true on each scatter's X (probes 34, 36, 38), the matrix's Region flipped active with expansionStates where the user expanded it (the slicer was NOT expanded and has no expansionStates, yet drew open to its regions: an active_levels: all hierarchy slicer is already in the expanded state), $schema 2.13.0 -> 2.14.0 on the files it rewrote, and pages.json activePageName. bp check reports no format findings, and re-applying the same specs over Desktop's save changed nothing at all, not even the manifest. All content invented.

